    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p>Bug Type: Functional / Data Inconsistency</p>

<p>Priority: Medium</p>

<p>Preconditions:</p>

<ul>
	<li>Game is running.</li>
	<li>Player is currently in gameplay.</li>
	<li>Pyrois character is selected.</li>
	<li>README documentation containing Pyrois's character stats and special skill description is available.</li>
</ul>


<p>Steps to Reproduce:</p>

<ol>
	<li>Open the README documentation.</li>
	<li>Locate the Pyrois character entry.</li>
	<li>Review the documented character attributes, including Speed, HP, Armor, and Special Skill.</li>
	<li>Launch the game and enter gameplay as Pyrois.</li>
	<li>Observe the in-game HUD, including the HP indicators.</li>
	<li>Compare the character's in-game attributes with the corresponding information in the README.</li>
</ol>


<p>Expected Result:</p>

<ul>
	<li>Pyrois's in-game attributes match the values documented in the README.</li>
	<li>Character statistics, including Speed (150), HP (5), and Armor (4), are consistent between the game and documentation.</li>
	<li>The special skill description accurately reflects the skill's in-game behavior.</li>
</ul>


<p>Actual Result:</p>

<ul>
	<li>A discrepancy exists between the README documentation and the in-game representation of Pyrois.</li>
	<li>The in-game HUD displays 4 red heart icons and 4 blue shield-like icons, while the README specifies HP = 5 and Armor = 4.</li>
	<li>The displayed HP appears inconsistent with the documented HP value.</li>
</ul>


<p>Test Case Result:</p>

<ul>
	<li>FAIL</li>
	<li>Related Test Case: Character Stats Consistency Test</li>
</ul>


<p>Notes:</p>

<ul>
	<li>The discrepancy should be investigated to determine whether the in-game HP value is incorrect or the README documentation is outdated.</li>
	<li>Verify whether the red heart icons represent the character's current HP, maximum HP, or another gameplay value before confirming the root cause.</li>
</ul>

            <br/>
        </td>
